# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5.memetic-wikitext" "A roleless authority reads as an authority, not as colourless path text"

# OPERATOR'S RULING 2026-10-06: the seed's own law (`#/lar-uri`) gives the session form as
# `lar://alias:grant@host/...` — a role is the law's own shape, so a roleless authority
# (`lar://claude@lararium/...`) stands in TENSION with it, common in practice but not licensed by
# the seed. Ruled anyway, for the same reason the colourless-path ruling already stands: 56 of 65
# themes give the colourless path bucket no selector at all, so a roleless authority that falls
# into it reads as one flat run next to a role-ful authority's three parted leaves. The cure reuses
# the EXISTING leaf names (persona, the authority separator, place) — no role leaf fires, because
# none stands.

x lar://claude:scryer@lararium/the-map.reads.its-ground
